WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.480
Let's go next to Ryan from D.C.. Ryan from
D.C.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.610
What's going on?

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:07.710
Hey, David.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:10.510
I'm taking my call and a longtime listener.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.510
My pleasure.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:12.650
Thanks for taking the time.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:18.970
My question is kind of more of a philosophical
one around, like some general political philosophy.

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:25.999
I'm with Texas kind of becoming more purple,
potentially even being blue by, say, 20, 30

00:00:25.999 --> 00:00:31.759
ish, and then the potential of D.C. and Puerto
Rico gaining statehood, which would likely

00:00:31.759 --> 00:00:34.090
go, you know, the Democratic route.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:40.270
I think just by some of the general statistics
that we have currently, I'm wondering, you

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:44.250
know, what would be great about those scenarios
is that the right would have a very difficult

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.559
time winning the presidency ever again.

00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:53.050
But I'm wondering more from a philosophical
standpoint, what you think it would look like

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:58.999
if the Democrats were dominating election
after election in some kind of a one party

00:00:58.999 --> 00:00:59.999
system.

00:00:59.999 --> 00:01:04.940
Do you think that the moderates and the and
the more progressive would kind of split within

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.160
the Democratic Party and create new parties?

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.270
What would that America look like?

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.460
That's very hard to predict.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:14.550
And it's like I could make a prediction, but
we know that that, you know, it would essentially

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.770
be worthless because what do any of us really
know?

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:24.550
The one thing I think, though, is if indeed
Texas's population moves left such that Democrats

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:28.940
are really in contention nationally in Texas
or even win Texas.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:34.160
My guess is that Texas Republicans would move
to the left and be back in contention.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:41.180
It's sort of like, why do Massachusetts voters
who are quite left elect Republican governors

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:45.600
so frequently, well, they're not electing,
you know, Joni Ernst.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:51.250
They're electing people like William Weld
and Charlie Baker and others.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:55.340
Republicans in Massachusetts have moved left
in order to remain viable.

00:01:55.340 --> 00:02:00.420
So my my instinct is that what you would see
in Texas, if it really starts to seem like

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:05.680
a like a national Republican could win, is
that the Texas Republican Party would start

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:08.500
coming to the left and they would remain viable.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.950
And that would be good because we're we're
still moving to the left if that happens,

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:12.950
right?

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:16.940
Yeah, I think the Overton Window would kind
of continue to shift left.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:19.740
And and I think that would actually still
be a net positive.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:24.370
And, yes, you know, they would have to move
to the left just to survive.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:25.450
I completely agree.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:26.840
I think that's the most likely scenario.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:30.890
You know, people think, oh, just Democrats
will win Texas from here until forever.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:31.890
Well, OK.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:34.250
I mean, at some point that could happen.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:39.950
But you could also see Republicans re reinstate
their sort of 55 45 majority by just moving

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:41.540
a little bit to the left.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:42.540
Brian.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.540
That's great.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:53.280
Yeah, was just something I was kind of thinking
about and wanted to kind of bounce it off,

00:02:53.280 --> 00:03:04.440
you suggested we call David.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:25.270
My pleasure.

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:30.230
All right.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:39.150
Thank you so much.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:57.720
Great to hear from 

